# ============================================================
# Rust / Cargo
# ============================================================
/target

# `.cargo/config.toml` is build-critical and IS committed: it points the `pcap`
# crate at the Npcap SDK on Windows and raises RUST_MIN_STACK so `cargo test`
# does not die in codegen. Ignoring the whole directory made every fresh clone
# fail to build. Only the credential file is secret.
.cargo/credentials
.cargo/credentials.toml
*.rlib

# ============================================================
# Node.js / npm
# ============================================================
node_modules/
desktop/node_modules
desktop/dist
desktop/frontend-tests/node_modules

# ============================================================
# Tauri
# ============================================================
desktop/src-tauri/version.conf.json
desktop/src-tauri/target

# ============================================================
# Distribution artifacts
# ============================================================
/dist/
dist/

# ============================================================
# Network captures (hassas trafik verisi içerebilir)
# ============================================================
*.pcap
*.pcapng
*.cap

# …except the test fixtures, which are synthetic (generated by
# `tools/gen-fixtures`), contain no real traffic, and are required by
# `crates/core/tests/integration_test.rs`.
!fixtures/*.pcap

# ============================================================
# Environment / Yerel yapılandırma (API key, token, şifre vs.)
# ============================================================
.env
.env.*
# The template is documentation, not configuration — it lists the variables
# without any values, so it is committed.
!.env.example
*.local.toml
secrets.toml
credentials.json
credentials.toml
service-account.json
service-account*.json
*.private-key.pem
*.secret

